WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:01.619
Happy birthday!

00:00:01.619 --> 00:00:07.299
It’s your day to enjoy however you want,
with lots of gifts and sweets.

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:10.530
And look - a little friend is here to help
you celebrate.

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:15.260
It’s the birthday monkey, and he has a song
to sing…

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:21.600
Dating back to the 1940s, SCP-983 is one of
the most harmless-looking objects in the SCP

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:22.840
Foundation’s possession.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:28.050
It’s an old-fashioned mechanical monkey,
a common wind-up toy from the old days.

00:00:28.050 --> 00:00:33.440
It’s dressed in a sharp little vest, and
holds a tiny bell and striking rod for making

00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:34.440
music.

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:39.180
It seems to be a simple toy, the kind that
would annoy a tired parent as it plays its

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:42.910
little tune over and over, but nothing more.

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:47.100
But this is no ordinary wind-up toy.

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:52.450
SCP-983 is capable of sounds and even speech
that doesn’t seem to match up with its design,

00:00:52.450 --> 00:00:57.850
and an investigation reveals it doesn’t
have any signs as to how it was constructed.

00:00:57.850 --> 00:01:03.510
No screws, seams, or markings that would be
common on a toy, and no voice box or other

00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:06.979
mechanical feature that would allow for speech.

00:01:06.979 --> 00:01:12.300
But despite these oddities, it seems to be
a normal toy that can be handled safely and

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:13.429
played with.

00:01:13.429 --> 00:01:17.140
On every day but one... that is.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:25.819
Because SCP-983 has a secondary purpose, and
on one special day it has a gift for its handler.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:29.819
It can be a gift of joy - or a gift of terror.

00:01:29.819 --> 00:01:36.310
Nicknamed the Birthday Monkey, SCP-983 activates
when it is handled by someone within the twenty-four

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.549
hour period of their birthday.

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:43.110
It seems to be able to tell when this period
of time happens automatically, and as soon

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:49.499
as it becomes aware, a series of surprises
begin to surface for the lucky - or unlucky

00:01:49.499 --> 00:01:50.499
- handler.

00:01:50.499 --> 00:01:53.600
It all starts with a little leap.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:59.170
As soon as SCP-983 becomes aware of the birthday
boy or girl, it’ll do a charming little

00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:00.170
backflip.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:05.420
It’ll then lift its bell and start singing
the same song - “A Ring Ding Ding Ding It’s

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:06.749
Your Birthday!”

00:02:06.749 --> 00:02:11.220
To this day, the Foundation has not been able
to figure out exactly where this voice comes

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:14.530
from, and it follows this by ringing its bell.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:19.260
The tone of the bell varies wildly - in ways
that the instrument should not be able to

00:02:19.260 --> 00:02:23.950
create, ranging from low tones to painfully
high-pitched tones.

00:02:23.950 --> 00:02:26.569
And that’s where the horror begins.

00:02:26.569 --> 00:02:31.930
The Birthday Monkey doesn’t just want to
sing a song - it wants to play a game.

00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:36.900
The song will repeat every three to four seconds,
marked by rings of the bell.

00:02:36.900 --> 00:02:42.720
And for every ring of the bell, the birthday
boy or girl will age a year - continuing until

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:46.840
they die of old age, or win the game.

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:50.060
But how does one win the game before it’s
too late?

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:55.090
No one is sure, but studies of this strange
toy in action indicate that it involves singing

00:02:55.090 --> 00:02:57.520
along - and timing it correctly.

00:02:57.520 --> 00:03:02.709
It’s probably a little hard to do that while
aging to death in seconds, but no one said

00:03:02.709 --> 00:03:05.250
SCPs play fair.

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:09.340
But in the event that someone actually does
manage to survive the Birthday Monkey’s

00:03:09.340 --> 00:03:12.170
game, it has a prize for them.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:18.469
When the sing-along is complete, SCP-983 will
let out an enthusiastic shout of “Birthday!”,

00:03:18.469 --> 00:03:22.209
ring its bell, and drop a single gumdrop from
its bell.

00:03:22.209 --> 00:03:26.659
But which gumdrop depends on just how well
the birthday victim did.

00:03:26.659 --> 00:03:30.400
A perfect sing-along will result in a clear
candy that seems to glow.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:34.980
If it’s a little less than perfect, the
candy won’t glow, but it’ll work the same

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:38.629
- and both candies have a very valuable property.

00:03:38.629 --> 00:03:43.799
When eaten, the candy will immediately reverse
any age lost during the “game”.

00:03:43.799 --> 00:03:47.310
But does the perfect score give another prize?

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:51.190
Studies of the rare glowing candy led the
Foundation to believe that it may also provide

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:56.640
a bonus effect, making the person who eats
it younger and giving them a longer lifespan

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:58.200
or better health.

00:03:58.200 --> 00:04:03.299
But this is largely guesswork, because the
candy is produced so rarely and the effects

00:04:03.299 --> 00:04:07.030
would only become clear after years or decades
of study.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:10.220
But not all candies are to be eaten.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:14.060
Many candies of different appearance and quality
have been produced.

00:04:14.060 --> 00:04:21.320
All can be eaten safely - except the black
ones, which represent a failed sing-along.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:26.780
The effects of this candy were discovered
the hard way - because the first time SCP-983

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:33.069
was activated, it was activated in the wild,
before the Foundation had secured it.

00:04:33.069 --> 00:04:38.150
And everyone knows that an SCP in the wild
can be a terrible thing.

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:42.889
It was a local flea market, when the buyer
noticed the sharp-dressed little monkey.

00:04:42.889 --> 00:04:47.449
The buyer, having a friend who loved monkeys,
thought this would be a perfect gift.

00:04:47.449 --> 00:04:51.860
The seller was not as enthusiastic, and warned
the buyer that it shouldn’t be handled or

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:54.389
even seen by anyone on their birthday.

00:04:54.389 --> 00:04:58.270
But even the seller didn’t really believe
this, saying that it might have just been

00:04:58.270 --> 00:05:01.550
an old legend that had been passed down for
years.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:06.509
It didn’t dissuade the buyer, and off the
monkey went to its new home.

00:05:06.509 --> 00:05:12.340
SCP-983 was activated at an office party,
where the monkey was presented as a gift.

00:05:12.340 --> 00:05:16.669
The guest of honor loved it at first - until
it started singing.

00:05:16.669 --> 00:05:21.470
The staff noticed that as the monkey kept
singing, their co-worker became more and more

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:22.750
upset.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:27.030
The monkey kept singing, and he started to
search for a way to turn it off - but there

00:05:27.030 --> 00:05:30.220
was no button or any other way to deactivate
it.

00:05:30.220 --> 00:05:34.080
And that’s when the coworkers noticed something
disturbing.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:38.550
The honoree seemed to be getting weaker and
weaker, and there were even streaks of grey

00:05:38.550 --> 00:05:40.470
appearing in his hair.

00:05:40.470 --> 00:05:43.509
His skin was getting more wrinkled and weathered.

00:05:43.509 --> 00:05:48.569
Soon his hair was entirely grey, and he simply
returned the monkey to where it was as it

00:05:48.569 --> 00:05:50.440
continued to sing.

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:55.900
He seemed to give up, begged for someone to
turn it off, and waited to expire.

00:05:55.900 --> 00:06:00.789
By the time the Foundation arrived on scene,
it was already too late.

00:06:00.789 --> 00:06:06.000
There was nothing left of the birthday boy
but a desiccated, skeletal corpse.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:11.310
The monkey had been able to sing at least
thirty more verses, and no one had truly understood

00:06:11.310 --> 00:06:13.030
what was going on.

00:06:13.030 --> 00:06:18.250
They reacted with confusion and inaction,
unable to contain the monkey’s dangerous

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:19.270
game.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:25.030
Even the Foundation didn’t understand SCP-983
at first, so they let the object continue

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:28.930
singing until the body degraded into a simple
skeleton.

00:06:28.930 --> 00:06:34.370
That’s when the monkey exclaimed its finishing
phrase and released a single black gumdrop.

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:39.640
While no one ate the gumdrop, the Foundation
observed that it seemed to hypnotize people

00:06:39.640 --> 00:06:44.100
around it, as if it was compelling them to
do something.

00:06:44.100 --> 00:06:49.930
What is lurking within the black gumdrops
- and do they want to be consumed?

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:54.990
The birthday monkey was taken into SCP custody,
and it became clear that it was harmless to

00:06:54.990 --> 00:06:58.560
everyone for 364 days of the year.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:07:03.680
The foundation wanted to understand more about
this odd toy, so they fell back on their best

00:07:03.680 --> 00:07:09.010
resource for testing - D-class personnel,
who got the chance to show off their singing

00:07:09.010 --> 00:07:13.660
skills with much higher stakes than your average
round of karaoke.

00:07:13.660 --> 00:07:18.410
Most of the tests were routine, with controlled
activations showing how to deactivate the

00:07:18.410 --> 00:07:23.360
monkey - or providing up-close studies of
its devastating effects.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.150
But one test hinted that this specimen could
be more dangerous than thought.

00:07:28.150 --> 00:07:33.050
Few people volunteer for testing duty at the
SCP Foundation, but that wasn’t the case

00:07:33.050 --> 00:07:35.449
for one now-classified subject.

00:07:35.449 --> 00:07:40.960
Her birthday was approaching, and she surprisingly
volunteered for the test that could only be

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:43.330
done on your birthday.

00:07:43.330 --> 00:07:48.479
She had an oddly upbeat attitude and seemed
oddly excited about her birthday.

00:07:48.479 --> 00:07:52.150
The test was approved, and she was given limited
information.

00:07:52.150 --> 00:07:56.990
She was given the monkey as a wrapped gift,
told it would sing, and encouraged to sing

00:07:56.990 --> 00:07:58.210
along for a video.

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:02.370
But her reaction indicated she might know
more than expected.

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:06.849
As soon as the gift was unwrapped, the SCP
began singing.

00:08:06.849 --> 00:08:10.640
After missing the first verse, the subject
picked up the words and started singing along

00:08:10.640 --> 00:08:16.010
- not just competently, but perfectly and
enthusiastically.

00:08:16.010 --> 00:08:20.770
Soon enough, she started aging rapidly, but
didn’t seem distressed by this at all.

00:08:20.770 --> 00:08:26.500
She maintained her high level of enthusiasm,
even as the monkey sang for over forty verses

00:08:26.500 --> 00:08:29.259
and aged her over forty years.

00:08:29.259 --> 00:08:33.960
She seemed unaware of these drastic changes,
and never missed a beat of the song until

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:37.450
the monkey issued its finishing exclamation.

00:08:37.450 --> 00:08:40.680
And now, it was time for her prize.

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:45.870
The gumdrop that fell from the bell was a
new one, completely white and almost shockingly

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:46.870
bright.

00:08:46.870 --> 00:08:51.140
It glowed, and the subject was immediately
enchanted by it.

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:56.190
Even the attending scientists and staff couldn’t
help but comment on how impressive it was.

00:08:56.190 --> 00:09:01.120
The subject was allowed to consume it to see
its effects, and was monitored for an hour

00:09:01.120 --> 00:09:02.120
afterward.

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:06.570
When nothing unusual happened besides the
reversal of the aging, the subject was excused

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:08.680
to return to her quarters.

00:09:08.680 --> 00:09:11.870
And that’s when things took a shocking turn.

00:09:11.870 --> 00:09:16.850
In an effect never seen before, the subject
suddenly exploded with a brilliant burst of

00:09:16.850 --> 00:09:18.210
white light.

00:09:18.210 --> 00:09:23.589
Whatever this light was, it was strong enough
to knock out all the cameras in the vicinity.

00:09:23.589 --> 00:09:28.230
Everyone in her presence was temporarily blinded,
with it taking five minutes for their eyesight

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:29.480
to return.

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:33.970
No long-term ill effects were shown, but the
staff that entered the room after the blast

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:36.420
noticed that an odd glow remained in the room.

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:39.900
And that wasn’t the only odd thing.

00:09:39.900 --> 00:09:45.750
The test subject was nowhere to be found - and
has never been seen again.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:50.390
The Foundation is on high alert for this test
subject, but she seems to be staying below

00:09:50.390 --> 00:09:53.630
the radar - if she’s even human at all anymore.

00:09:53.630 --> 00:09:58.990
While there is no physical sign of her, the
Foundation has observed odd patterns of electromagnetic

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:04.430
activity in the area and is following reports
of light fixtures needing to be replaced.

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:09.560
It was clear that SCP-983 was much more unpredictable
than expected.

00:10:09.560 --> 00:10:15.490
While still classified as safe, the Foundation
is keeping SCP-983 under tighter lock and

00:10:15.490 --> 00:10:17.110
key these days.

00:10:17.110 --> 00:10:21.620
All technicians who handle it are carefully
vetted to ensure they are nowhere near their

00:10:21.620 --> 00:10:22.620
birthday.

00:10:22.620 --> 00:10:27.520
In case of accidental exposure, the Foundation
has prepared emergency kits with detailed

00:10:27.520 --> 00:10:32.270
instructions for how to complete the Birthday
Monkey’s deadly sing-along game.

00:10:32.270 --> 00:10:37.389
But as with all things, the Foundation is
prepared for anything.

00:10:37.389 --> 00:10:42.220
In the event of a failure, the remains will
be disposed of by vetted staff.

00:10:42.220 --> 00:10:46.760
Any candies produced are to be taken into
custody by the Foundation and studied for

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:52.829
unusual properties, but are not to be consumed
without full containment procedures and approval

00:10:52.829 --> 00:10:54.579
from senior staff.

00:10:54.579 --> 00:11:02.020
The only exception is D-class testing - but
even in those cases, one rule remains intact.

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:05.889
No one is ever to consume the black candies.

00:11:05.889 --> 00:11:11.029
And caution is encouraged around the Birthday
Monkey - lest you wind up in a sing-along

00:11:11.029 --> 00:11:12.580
for your life.

00:11:12.580 --> 00:11:18.080
For more on an ordinary object with unique
properties, check out “SCP-978 - Desire

00:11:18.080 --> 00:11:23.660
Camera”, or watch “SCP-342 - A Ticket
to Ride” for another particularly tricky

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:23.819
trap.

